 * so nothing here stopped this root from being pushed wider than its
 * intended column the moment it held content with a wider minimum than
 * hidden inputs (whose own minimum is zero). `w-full` is the complementary
 * half: it makes the root explicitly claim exactly its column's width rather
 * than an undefined natural one, so it can only ever match the column, never
