            <?php
            /*
             * TWO-25326: the order-intent check had no
             * visible progress indicator at all on Hyvä, so a buyer who picked
             * a company sat looking at an unchanged tile for however long the
             * decision took and had no way to tell it was working.
             *
             * LOCAL to the tile, never a page overlay — the standing
             * cross-platform rule, and the same reason the company-search
             * spinner is an in-field element rather than
             * `magewire:loader:start`: a full-screen overlay over a checkout
             * the buyer is still filling in blocks interaction for a background
             * check they did not ask for. This element sits in the tile's own
             * flow, exactly where the verdict will appear a moment later, so it
             * is replaced by its own result rather than by nothing.
             *
             * `role="status"` and a real text label, not a bare spinner: the two
             * notices it precedes are announced the same way, and a decorative
             * GIF alone tells a screen-reader user nothing at all. The GIF is
             * `.two-company-search__spinner`, the same asset and the same
             * childless-element mechanism the search field uses — it is
             * positioned absolutely against this row.
             *
             * Rendered in BOTH company-search-location modes: the intent check
             * runs whichever surface captured the company.
             *
             * The box (border, radius, padding, colour) is `custom.css`'s, not
             * Tailwind utilities': it is one of four states of ONE box — this
             * row and the three verdicts below it — and the four have to agree
             * on their geometry, which they cannot do if each restates it in a
             * class list. The same reason
             * `.two-company-search__unavailable` is CSS here rather than a
             * utility: the module must not depend on the merchant's Tailwind
             * build having generated a colour only this module asks for, and an
             * uncompiled `bg-red-50` is an invisible box rather than a loud
             * failure.
             */
            ?>
            <div
                class="two-order-intent-box two-order-intent-checking"
                x-cloak
                role="status"
                data-name="order_intent_checking"
                x-show="orderIntentChecking"
            >
                <span><?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Checking availability')) ?></span>
                <span class="two-company-search__spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </div>
            <?php
            /*
             * Persistent inline "order intent approved" notice, inside the
             * payment tile. Replaces the window.dispatchMessages() toast,
             * which was visible but self-dismissed after 5 seconds — long
             * before a buyer still filling in the form had any use for it.
             *
             * Emitted only when the brand has not switched the notice off, so
             * a suppressing brand yields no element at all rather than a
             * permanently hidden wrapper. Class name matches the Luma,
             * WooCommerce and PrestaShop surfaces so the four checkout
             * treatments stay greppable; the Tailwind utilities alongside it
             * follow the same idiom as the payment-terms box below.
             *
             * It sits inside the form's Alpine scope, not the outer tile's,
             * because the form is the instance that runs initialize() and so
             * the one holding the order-intent state.
             *
             * `x-show` reads `orderIntentMessageVisible` rather than the notice
             * text directly — same truth value, but it makes the shared gate
             * literal: the company label above reads the identical getter, so
             * the two cannot drift apart. `x-text` still reads the text.
