                    role="status"
                    data-name="order_intent_message"
                    x-show="orderIntentMessageVisible"
                    x-text="orderIntentApprovedNotice"
                ></div>
            <?php endif ?>
            <?php
            /*
             * TWO-25326: the sibling "not approved / no intent" text. Same
             * shape and same reasoning as the approved notice above — a
             * persistent inline element rather than a toast, gated on the
             * identical brand switch (see
             * CheckoutConfig::getOrderIntentNotAvailableNotice()) — but its own
             * element, because it needs its own (unavailable, not success)
             * styling and its own `x-text`.
             *
             * Rendered in BOTH company-search-location modes, not only the
             * text-only tile: it is the ENTIRE story for a declined/no-intent
             * company on either surface. It is also the only notice — the
             * 5-second decline toast that used to fire alongside it is gone,
             * so one verdict produces exactly one notice.
             *
             * Which makes the CONDITION on this element load-bearing beyond
             * this file: when the brand switch suppresses the copy there is no
             * element here at all, so `processOrderIntentSuccessResponse()`
             * falls back to a toast for a decline that has no sentence to show.
             *
             * The two conditions are deliberately NOT the same test. This one
             * decides whether the ELEMENT exists
             * (`getOrderIntentNotAvailableNotice() !== null`); the JS one asks
             * the wider question, whether there is a SENTENCE
             * (`resolveOrderIntentNotAvailableNotice() === ''`), which is also
             * true for copy that is present but unusable and would otherwise
             * render this element empty and silent. Absent copy is the case
             * where both agree, and it is the case this condition exists for.
             */
            ?>
            <?php if ($configModel->getOrderIntentNotAvailableNotice() !== null): ?>
                <div
                    class="two-order-intent-box two-order-intent-message unavailable"
                    x-cloak
                    role="status"
                    data-name="order_intent_not_available_message"
